-- title:
--   Formal smoothness of a one-dimensional local domain over a perfect field
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a perfect field and let $\mathcal{O}$ be a commutative ring which is local, a domain and Noetherian, equipped with a $K$-algebra structure making it essentially of finite type over $K$ (i.e. a localisation of a finitely generated $K$-algebra, in the sense of `Algebra.EssFiniteType`). Suppose there is an element $u \in \mathcal{O}$ with $u \neq 0$ such that the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}$ is the principal ideal generated by $u$. Then the structure morphism $K \to \mathcal{O}$ is formally smooth, i.e. for every surjection of $K$-algebras with square-zero (indeed nilpotent) kernel, every $K$-algebra map from $\mathcal{O}$ to the quotient lifts to the source. No hypothesis is imposed on the residue field $\mathcal{O}/(u)$ beyond what follows from essential finite type over $K$; in particular it may be a transcendental extension of $K$, so the statement covers the local ring at a codimension-one point that is not closed.
--
--   This is the case of a perfect base field of the implication "regular $\Rightarrow$ smooth" in dimension one: a Noetherian local domain with principal nonzero maximal ideal, essentially of finite type over a perfect field, is formally smooth over that field. It is used in the project to prove smoothness of one-dimensional integrally closed algebras over perfect fields, to recognise points of the smooth locus of a morphism of schemes from regularity of the stalk, and in a statement that a localisation of a tensor product at a prime is a domain.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Algebra_FormallySmooth_of_maximalIdeal_eq_span_of_perfectField.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u v

open IsLocalRing

theorem Algebra.FormallySmooth.of_maximalIdeal_eq_span_of_perfectField
    (K : Type u) [Field K] [PerfectField K] (𝒪 : Type v) [CommRing 𝒪] [IsLocalRing 𝒪] [IsDomain 𝒪] [IsNoetherianRing 𝒪]
    [Algebra K 𝒪] [Algebra.EssFiniteType K 𝒪]
    (u : 𝒪) (hu0 : u ≠ 0) (hu : maximalIdeal 𝒪 = Ideal.span {u}) :
    Algebra.FormallySmooth K 𝒪 := by sorry
